Fune for the Cardputer Zero -- Alpha, for M5Stack's emulator (@OS@)
=====================================================================

Fune is a groovebox: 4 tracks of synths and drums, a step sequencer, effects.
This is the Cardputer Zero version, run inside M5Stack's Cardputer Zero emulator
(the device's screen, 320 x 170, and its keyboard on your computer).

ALPHA: tested in the emulator only, not on a Cardputer Zero. Things will break.

1. Get M5Stack's emulator (MIT licence, not included here)
   https://github.com/CardputerZero/Emulator/releases
   @EMU_HOWTO@

2. Start Fune in it
   Unzip this folder anywhere, then in a terminal:
     cd @DIR@
     ./run.sh
   run.sh looks for the emulator @EMU_WHERE@;
   elsewhere: CZEMU=/path/to/the/emulator ./run.sh
   (By hand: <emulator>/cardputer-emu /full/path/to/@LIB@)

Keys (click the keys on the picture, or type on your keyboard)
  F Z X C          cursor up, left, down, right (the orange arrows, no fn needed)
  K L              value up / down
  1 .. 0           pages: 1 HOME (mixer), 2 SEQ, 3 GLO, 4 SYNTH, 5 EDIT, 6 ENV, 7 LFO, 8 FX, 9 ARP, 0 every page
                   (the same key again: the next page of its group)
  OK (Return)      yes        del (Backspace)  no
  Space            play / stop
  ESC, HOME        back
  , .              ALGORITHM: the pattern on SEQ, the engine, the effect, the settings' tabs
  r REC   s SAVE   g settings   u undo   t tools   o p presets   [ ] octave
  On the mixer (HOME): left / right the track, up / down its control.
  SAVE: stop playback first ("Stop to save"). The song saved last opens at the next start.

Files
  Songs, presets and settings are kept in @DATA@
  (the same folder Fune's desktop build uses).
Sound: your computer's default output. MIDI: @MIDI@.

Known limits
  - Alpha, emulator only: the real device's speed, sound (ALSA) and keyboard are untested.
  - Built against the emulator v1.0.0 (@EMU_REV@, LVGL 9.5); other emulator versions may not load it.
  - Clicking the picture's keys very fast can drop a key.
  - Quitting: close the emulator's window. Unsaved changes are lost (no auto-save).

Fune @VERSION@, built @DATE@. Open source: MPL-2.0 (LICENSE.txt, LICENSING.md); the source at
https://github.com/hugelton/Fune. Others' parts and their licences: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.

